The proposed solution must provide hospital staff with quick access to reliable and up-to-date information drawn from internal procedures, care protocols, and applicable regulatory texts. It will assist in drafting medical and administrative documents, support dossier handling, and facilitate continuity of care between professionals and services. Our solution will not introduce a rupture in clinical or administrative workflows and will fit into existing practices.

In terms of technical requirements, our platform's performance metrics indicate response times below 2 seconds for common queries, meeting the requirement for high availability, including outside office hours. We will utilize standard connectors for SIH and DPI integration and provide custom adapters where needed. Our sovereign HDS tier hosting option is certified to the required standards, including SecNumCloud-qualified and HDS-certified, and is located within the EU.

We guarantee strict compliance with GDPR, processing health data as special-category data (GDPR Art. 9), and preserving medical confidentiality (secret médical). Data will be hosted exclusively within the European Union, with no transfer outside the EU authorized. Sensitive data will be protected by encryption and pseudonymisation where relevant.

Our solution provides explainability and traceability of recommendations or suggestions produced, with source grounding, audit trail, and support for a posteriori review. It supports medical coding (PMSI/ICD-10) for activity reporting (T2A) and considers dossier context where available. No decision will be automated without explicit validation by a qualified professional.

