Our solution will be hosted on a sovereign HDS tier infrastructure, utilizing a fully sovereign European open-weight model, avoiding dependency on non-European suppliers. We have experience in delivering solutions that comply with GDPR, particularly for public sector and health clients, including special-category health data.

In terms of budget constraints, the global budget allocated to the project is estimated at €900,000 over 5 years. Our standard daily rates range from €700 to €1,300 per day, depending on the role. We will optimize costs while guaranteeing the expected quality of service, ensuring that annual operating costs remain controlled and compatible with the authority's budgetary capacity.

Finally, our solution contributes to reducing energy consumption and relies on low-carbon infrastructure, aligning with CHRB's sustainable development policy. We prioritize responsible tech through our charter signatory status, promoting gender balance and inclusion objectives, apprenticeship and work-study programs, and research partnerships with institutions like the Grenoble research ecosystem.

We believe that our consortium has a strong capability to deliver this project within the specified timeframe and budget, providing a high-quality solution that meets the requirements of the Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval.
